          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+category"} localization of a category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} of an (∞,1)-category
            is called
            %strong reflective
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+functor"} localization functor
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            = succeed "-inclusion." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} reflective sub-(∞,1)-category
          %p
            In fact every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            inclusion exhibits a reflective localization (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveSubcategoriesAreLocalizations"}
            below).
          %p
            For reflective localizations the localized category has a particularly useful description (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveLocalizationGivenByLocalObjects"}
            below): It is equivalent to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalObjects"}
            below).
          %p
            Therefore, sometimes reflective localizations at a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of morphisms are understood as the default concept of localization, in fact often reflection onto the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizationAtACollectionOfMorphisms"}
            below) is understood by default. Notably
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Bousfield+localizations"} left Bousfield localizations
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            of reflective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizations+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} localizations of (∞,1)-categories
            in this sense.
          %p
            These reflections onto
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            (only) for all
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            functors that invert the class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectionOntoLocalObjectsIsLocalizationWithRespectToLeftAdjoints"}
            below).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#ReflectiveLoc Reflective localization
          #CategoryWithWeakEquivalences.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"}> category with weak equivalences
                )
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} category with weak equivalences
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset \mathcal{C}
            %p
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  include all the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  satisfy
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/two-out-of-three"} two-out-of-three
                %p
                  If for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
