          %h3#ReflectionOntoLocalObjects Reflection onto local objects
          %p
            It turns out (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReflectiveLocalizationGivenByLocalObjects"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are, when they exist,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflections
            onto the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalObjects"}
            below). Often this reflection of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
            is what one is more interested in than the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            according to (Def.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryWithWeakEquivalences"}
            %em reflection onto local objects
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalizationAtACollectionOfMorphisms"}
            below) is what is often meant by default with “localization” (for instance in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
          #LocalObjects.num_defn
